Purpose: three changes to CrowdSurf's throughput benchmark, merged into one
patch because they touch adjacent regions of the same function.

1. Respect the `-batch N` CLI flag instead of iterating the hardcoded
   `ks = {1, 8, 32, ..., 2048}`. Upstream ignores `-batch` in throughput mode
   and always sweeps all nine sizes.

2. Add a `-batches 1,2,4,...` flag for sweeps. The DB generation and hint
   computation above the loop are the dominant cost (~10 min at 4 GiB), so a
   batch-scaling sweep must stay inside one invocation rather than re-invoking
   the binary per point.

3. Replace `testing.Benchmark` with an explicit 10-trial loop. Upstream reports
   only an averaged throughput over an auto-scaled iteration count; timing each
   `Answer` separately gives per-trial times and a real standard deviation,
   matching SandwichPIR's `allServerTimesMs` convention. Emits a
   machine-parseable `TrialsMs(...): t1, t2, ...` line alongside the existing
   `Throughput(...)` line.

Apply with: patch -l -p1 -d schemes/distpir < patches/03-distpir-bench-harness.patch

